<!-- Author: Chrissy Safranski  -->

<setup>
  <function name="r">(x^2-1)/(x^2-3x-4)</function>
</setup>
<p>
  Consider the rational function <m>r(x) = \frac{x^2 - 1}{x^2 - 3x - 4}</m>, and let <m>p(x) = x^2 - 1</m> and <m>q(x) = x^2 - 3x - 4</m>.  Note that <m>p(x)</m> is the numerator of <m>r(x)</m> and <m>q(x)</m> is the denominator of <m>r(x)</m>.
</p>

    <p>
      <answer><mathInput name="mi1"><label>Reasoning algebraically, for what values of <m>x</m> is <m>p(x) = 0</m>?</label><description>To enter a list of numbers, separate the numbers with commas.</description></mathInput><award><when><mathList>$mi1</mathList>=<mathList unordered>1 -1</mathList></when></award></answer>
    </p>
    <p>
       <answer><mathInput name="mi2"><label>Again reasoning algebraically, for what values of <m>x</m> is <m>q(x) = 0</m>?</label><description>To enter a list of numbers, separate the numbers with commas.</description></mathInput><award><when><mathList>$mi2</mathList>=<mathList unordered>4 -1</mathList></when></award></answer>
    </p>
    <p>
      Type <m>r(x)</m> in the box below, and the following table values will automatically fill in.
    </p>
    <p>
      <answer><mathInput name="rEnt"><label><m>r(x)=</m></label></mathInput><award><when>$rEnt=$r</when></award></answer>
    </p>
